omnigraph cleanup: take __manifest version numbers from the listing.

Backport of https://github.com/ModernRelay/omnigraph/pull/1188 (merge commit
269299b757f9dcce1a9a45449ebbaefa054b4be3) onto the v0.14.0 tag
(60bfd19db780fdff3a5178f959c1204143420114). Stock v0.14.0 cleanup reads and
decodes every __manifest version of every live branch, one at a time, on every
run. With this, every policy takes version numbers from the _versions/ listing:
--keep N alone reads only the manifests it retains and the merge base, and
--older-than reads the versions its cutoff decides, concurrently. It also
changes two refusals: --keep N alone prunes a dropped commit whose manifest
can't be read instead of stopping, and a listed version whose manifest body
names another version is refused.

Its crates/ hunks apply to v0.14.0 as they are (three at line offsets), and touch
none of the files omnigraph-cli-inline-s3-root.patch does, so this is that diff
regenerated against the tag. Its docs/ and changelog.d/ hunks are left out.

docker/omnigraph-server.Dockerfile's cli-patched stage applies it with
`git apply`, which skips this header. Delete this file, and its COPY and
`git apply` lines, once the release the Dockerfile's OMNIGRAPH_RELEASE_TAG pins
carries #1188.

